        <title type="html"><![CDATA[`position-area`: add behavioral subfeature for auto margins]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29280</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29280"/>
        <updated>2026-03-17T14:40:32.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64103?u=428d3c27c9cd7efc648e17dfe5a4321c3f8e44d2&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">A specification change to anchor positioning now requires that if a non-<code class="notranslate">none</code> <code class="notranslate">position-area</code> applies to an element, then <code class="notranslate">margin: auto</code> and <code class="notranslate">inset: auto</code> to <a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-anchor-position/#:~:text=available%0Afor%20positioning.-,the%20used%20value%20of%20any%20auto%20inset%20properties%20and%20auto%20margin%20properties%20resolves%20to%200.,-The%20normal%20value" rel="nofollow">resolve to 0</a>. This PR captures support for this behavior in a behavior subfeature.</p>

<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<h5 dir="auto">Spec</h5>
<p dir="auto">The spec text is <a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-anchor-position/#:~:text=available%0Afor%20positioning.-,the%20used%20value%20of%20any%20auto%20inset%20properties%20and%20auto%20margin%20properties%20resolves%20to%200.,-The%20normal%20value" rel="nofollow">this bullet point</a>:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">The used value of any 'auto' inset properties and 'auto' margin properties resolves to '0'.</p>
</blockquote>
<p dir="auto">It followed <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2266340227" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10258" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10258/hovercard?comment_id=3407160892&amp;comment_type=issue_comment" href="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10258#issuecomment-3407160892">w3c/csswg-drafts#10258 (comment)</a>.</p>
<h5 dir="auto">Chrome</h5>
<p dir="auto">According to <a href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/374574260#comment18" rel="nofollow">bug 374574260 (comment #18)</a> Chrome appears to have supported this behavior—or something close it—in its initial anchor positioning implementation. Then the spec changed <em>twice</em>, bringing back this original behavior.</p>
<h5 dir="auto">Firefox</h5>
<p dir="auto">The actual support for this comes out of <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1997481" rel="nofollow">Firefox bug 1997481</a>, though the changes to make the test pass came about in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2006398" rel="nofollow">Firefox bug 2006398</a>.</p>
<h5 dir="auto">Safari</h5>
<p dir="auto"><a href="https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=300823" rel="nofollow">WebKit bug 300823</a> tracks this; it was fixed by <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3519663143" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/issues/52419" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/WebKit/WebKit/pull/52419/hovercard" href="https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/52419">WebKit/WebKit#52419</a>. I determined the version number where it ultimately shipped from the <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/safari-release-notes/safari-26_2-release-notes#:~:text=Fixed%20auto%20margins" rel="nofollow">Safari 26.2 Release Notes</a>.</p>


<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Via <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3647585549" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/3558" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/3558/hovercard" href="https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/3558">web-platform-dx/web-features#3558</a></li>
<li>Spec resolution: <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2266340227" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10258" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10258/hovercard?comment_id=3407160892&amp;comment_type=issue_comment" href="https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/10258#issuecomment-3407160892">w3c/csswg-drafts#10258 (comment)</a></li>
<li><a href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/374574260#comment18" rel="nofollow">Chromium bug 374574260 (comment #18)</a></li>
<li><a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1997481" rel="nofollow">Firefox bug 1997481</a> and <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2006398" rel="nofollow">bug 2006398</a></li>
<li><a href="https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=300823" rel="nofollow">WebKit bug 300823</a> and <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3519663143" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/issues/52419" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/WebKit/WebKit/pull/52419/hovercard" href="https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/52419">WebKit/WebKit#52419</a>.</li>
<li>Loosely related to <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4083024202" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29272" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29272/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29272">#29272</a></li>
</ul>

]]></content>
